From bc4346ebaf4114198c4dd7056bf6a6702fe6611d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:52:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] rephist: Pair opened-connection gauge decrements with
 open accounting

rep_hist_note_conn_opened() is only called from three places:
listener_connection_new() when a listener is created, and
note_connection() after an accepted connection passes
connection_init_accepted_conn() or an outbound socket finishes
connection_connect_sockaddr(). However, rep_hist_note_conn_closed() was
called unconditionally in connection_mark_for_close_internal_() using the
connection's current (from_listener, type, socket_family).

Several normal and flood-reachable lifecycles closed connections without
a matching increment or under a mutated type:
  - Accepted OR connections whose initial TLS handshake fails
    synchronously inside connection_init_accepted_conn() (when client
    FIN/RST or non-TLS bytes are already buffered at accept time) or
    transparent AP connections failing original-destination lookup are
    marked for close before note_connection() runs, pulling OR/received
    or Socks/received down toward 0.
  - Socketless linked connections (server-side EXIT + DIR pairs for
    BEGIN_DIR, client/self-fetch AP + DIR pairs from
    connection_ap_make_link(), and DNSPort AP connections) never call
    note_connection() but are closed via connection_mark_for_close(),
    pulling Exit/initiated, Directory/initiated, and Socks/initiated
    down toward 0.
  - Unconnected outbound DIR connections that fail connection_connect()
    and resolving EXIT streams closed before connection_exit_connect()
    similarly decrement without incrementing.
  - Extended ORPort connections are counted as CONN_TYPE_EXT_OR at
    accept, retyped to CONN_TYPE_OR in connection_ext_or_transition(),
    and decremented as CONN_TYPE_OR on close, leaving EXT_OR/received
    elevated while pulling OR/received down.

Record in_rephist_opened along with the counted direction, type, and
address family on connection_t whenever rep_hist_note_conn_opened() is
called, and only call rep_hist_note_conn_closed() (in
connection_mark_for_close_internal_() or connection_free_minimal()) when
in_rephist_opened is set.

Fixes #41350.
